# D-93, under --walk-methods: unit_make_adder_model_call.lm2's text, the first call before the
# model's definition (as the refused fixture had it).  The host is walked; its
# call of the model is the root's held call, l2_mad_call, over the node the model's PRIM builds at
# the call (l2_rw_mad_build) -- q 6, r 16, n 22, add(1) = 23.  Mutant: the walked call as an
# ordinary call of the model, over its occurrence and no node -- "walk error: INVALID", exit 3.
# Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    int: q (addN: 1)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    n: n + 10
    int: r (addN: 1)
    n: q + r
    return: addN

add: makeAdder 5
int: a (add: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 23
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
